# The playground wasm is a BUILD ARTIFACT: pages.yml builds it into static/
# before hugo runs. It was committed once, went 35 commits stale, and a CDN
# fallback served that stale copy to visitors. Never commit it again.
static/*.wasm

# `go build ./cmd/playground-wasm` with no -o drops a ~21 MB NATIVE binary here,
# named after the package directory. It was committed that way once (c7dbdd2) and
# every later build silently re-committed it. It is a build artifact; the wasm the
# site serves is built by pages.yml.
playground/playground-wasm
playground/git-worker
# The same binary lands in the COMMAND'S OWN directory when the build is run
# from inside it (`cd playground/cmd/git-worker && go build ./...`), which the
# two paths above do not cover — an 18 MB git-worker reached the index that way.
playground/cmd/playground-wasm/playground-wasm
playground/cmd/git-worker/git-worker
